Pathogenesis is poorly understood. Malassezia furfur (pityrosporum ovale), a lipophilic yeast that is a skin commensal is found in large numbers in involved skin. Reaction to the yeasts may play some part in the pathogenesis. Adult seborrhoeic dermatitis is chronic and recurrent. Parkinson disease and epilepsy predispose to seborrhoeic dermatitis. Patients with HIV/AIDS may have very severe disease. Although seborrhoeic dermatitis is not particularly itchy, it is disfiguring. Infantile seborrhoeic dermatitis is unrelated to the disease in adults (see E p. 602).  Pathogenesis is poorly understood. Malassezia furfur (pityrosporum ovale), a lipophilic yeast that is a skin commensal is found in large numbers in involved skin. Reaction to the yeasts may play some part in the pathogenesis. Adult seborrhoeic dermatitis is chronic and recurrent. Parkinson disease and epilepsy predispose to seborrhoeic dermatitis. Patients with HIV/AIDS may have very severe disease. Although seborrhoeic dermatitis is not particularly itchy, it is disfiguring. Infantile seborrhoeic dermatitis is unrelated to the disease in adults (see E p. 602).


