[Handbook: ehlers danlos syndrome]
Ehlers–​Danlos syndrome (EDS) is a heterogeneous spectrum of inherited disorders with overlapping clinical features that may include hyperextensible skin, hypermobile joints, and generalized tissue fragility. • Vascular EDS carries a high risk of life-threatening uterine or vascular rupture. EDS is caused by mutations in genes that modify collagen proteins (see Table 19.1).  Ehlers–​Danlos syndrome (EDS) is a heterogeneous spectrum of inherited disorders with overlapping clinical features that may include hyperextensible skin, hypermobile joints, and generalized tissue fragility. • Vascular EDS carries a high risk of life-threatening uterine or vascular rupture. EDS is caused by mutations in genes that modify collagen proteins (see Table 19.1).
