Synonym: Darier–​White disease.  Synonym: Darier–​White disease.  This autosomal dominantly inherited disease usually presents in childhood or adolescence and pursues a chronic, relapsing course. Prevalence is around 1 in 36 000. Mutations in ATP2A2, a gene encoding the endoplasmic reticulum calcium pump SERCA2, cause impaired keratinocyte adhesion (acantholysis) with dyskeratosis. Severe disfiguring and disabling disease may be linked to major depression.  This autosomal dominantly inherited disease usually presents in childhood or adolescence and pursues a chronic, relapsing course. Prevalence is around 1 in 36 000. Mutations in ATP2A2, a gene encoding the endoplasmic reticulum calcium pump SERCA2, cause impaired keratinocyte adhesion (acantholysis) with dyskeratosis. Severe disfiguring and disabling disease may be linked to major depression.
