 provide the most comprehensive match. The other diagnoses — sarcoidosis, kaposi sarcoma, actinic keratosis, and granuloma annulare — lack key features: sarcoidosis typically presents with yellowish-brown papules, kaposi sarcoma with vascular nodules, actinic keratosis with discrete scaly patches on sun-exposed skin, and granuloma annulare with annular plaques. No precedent cases were found, but the visual and guideline-based evidence is sufficient to support lichen planus as the most likely diagnosis.'}
