rance is consistent with the acute or subacute inflammatory process described in Behçet disease, and the absence of other features (like telangiectasia or pigment network) does not contradict the diagnosis, as these are not always present. Therefore, despite the low probability from the model, the visual and clinical evidence strongly supports Behçet disease as the most likely diagnosis."}
